# NON-SECRET settings for the PostgreSQL service of the compose example only.
#
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD - the password of the "postgres" superuser - is mandatory for the postgres image but
# is deliberately NOT declared here, because this file is tracked in the Apache OFBiz repository and a
# published superuser password would be a known credential in every checkout. docker-compose.yml
# references it as "${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:?...}", so Compose reads it from your environment and refuses to
# start the stack until you supply it. See "Examples of running the OFBiz container" in DOCKER.adoc.
#
# The file is kept - rather than deleted - so the compose service keeps ONE obvious place for any
# genuinely non-secret PostgreSQL setting the example may need later. A file of comments is a valid
# env_file.